From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Show NSOpenPanel/NSSavePanel for comdlg32 (native file dialogs).

MacSW lets Windows programs use the macOS file panels (patch 0024 makes
comdlg32 use them when MACSW_NATIVE_FILE_DIALOGS=1). This patch is the
driver side:

- cocoa_filedialog.m runs an NSOpenPanel/NSSavePanel described by a JSON
  request: title, prompt, start folder, file name, the Windows filters as a
  "Format" popup (open panels grey out non-matching files; save panels also
  get allowedFileTypes so NSSavePanel appends the extension before its own
  overwrite prompt), multi-select, folder picking, and an accessory view
  with the IFileDialogCustomize controls (check boxes, combo boxes, radio
  lists, text, edit boxes, separators, push buttons, menus, visual groups).
  The panel is a sheet on the owner's Cocoa window when it is on screen,
  otherwise a centred panel at the owner's level (at least normal), so a
  dialog that an accessory button opens comes up above it; the app asks to
  be activated. While such a button's handler runs the panel ignores the
  mouse ("busy" update).
- Save panels refuse names that Windows programs cannot create (\ / * ? "
  < > |, control characters, trailing dot or space). Filter extensions with
  wildcards or separators are not used as allowed types.
- Open panels test file names against the filters with their own matcher,
  not libc fnmatch (one fnmatch call once kept the main thread, and so the
  panel, busy for minutes): "*.ext" compares the suffix in any case; other
  patterns use '*' and '?' only, ASCII case folding, no locale, '[' and ']'
  literal. The answer is cached per (filter, file name) until the filter
  changes, and a shouldEnableURL call that takes more than 50 ms is logged
  (ERR) with the patterns and the name.
- The panel reports "started" once it is up. An exception while it is set
  up ends it without that line (comdlg32 then shows the Wine dialog);
  exceptions while applying updates are logged and dropped.
- The panel is asynchronous. Folder, selection, type and control changes and
  the final result are queued as text lines; updates from comdlg32 change
  controls, file name, Format and folder while it is up. The unix call
  (unix_file_dialog: begin, poll, update, cancel, release) never waits for
  the user, so the Windows thread keeps pumping messages.
- The PE side exports macsw_file_dialog() (winemac.drv.spec), which
  comdlg32 finds with GetProcAddress. The parameter block has the same
  layout for 32- and 64-bit callers, so the wow64 table uses the same entry.
- MACSW_NATIVE_FILE_DIALOG_TEST (automation only, passed in the request by
  comdlg32) ends the real panel after an optional delay with a given answer,
  after setting the Format popup and accessory controls as a user would; a
  save name the panel refuses ends it with cancel. Before an answer with
  paths it sends a folder line for the first path's folder and, in open
  panels, a selection line with the paths, then answers 500 ms later, as a
  user who goes to the file and clicks it.

Nothing here runs unless comdlg32 asks for a panel.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in b/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in
